def search_matrix_staircase(matrix, target):
    m, n = len(matrix), len(matrix[0])
    row, col = 0, n - 1               # start at the top-right corner
    while row < m and col >= 0:
        val = matrix[row][col]
        if val == target:
            return True
        elif val > target:
            col -= 1                  # eliminate this column entirely
        else:
            row += 1                  # eliminate this row entirely
    return False
```

Starting at the top-right corner is the only position where a single comparison eliminates either a whole row or a whole column outright: if the current value is too big, every value below it in the same column is also too big (columns are sorted downward); if it's too small, every value to its left in the same row is also too small (rows are sorted rightward).
